  "body": "I conjecture that open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle._plain_quotes gives the same answer for two replies that its documented rule requires it to tell apart. The documented rule is: “Fold typographic apostrophes and quotation marks to their ASCII forms.” The two replies are: “a‐b” (with U+2010 HYPHEN) and “a-b” (with ASCII hyphen). The rule mentions only typographic apostrophes and quotation marks, so it requires the check to preserve the difference between U+2010 and ASCII hyphen: the first should return “a‐b” and the second “a-b”. But I conjecture that the translation table _TYPOGRAPHIC_QUOTES erroneously includes U+2010 mapping to '-', so the check returns “a-b” for both. What would make me wrong: if _TYPOGRAPHIC_QUOTES does not contain U+2010, then the outputs would differ, and the check would tell the pair apart as the rule requires.",
